Hi Folks!

This is just a small program that my be expaded if people ask for.

What is it for?

It renumbers the users of TransAmiga BBS and also writes a new Users.BBS so
that next usernumbers are continued at the right place. The original order
is kept. Sometimes TransAmiga uses a usernumber twice. This happens when
your Amiga gurus or is resetted before a new user logged off.

I can not guarantee that this program will work on your environment so make
a BACKUP of your user directory.

The only thing you have to tell my program is the complete path to the
place where you keep the userfiles. When you use the suggested setup it is
BBS:Users . The path may end with a ':', '/' or noneof them. If none of
them is given my program adds a slash ('/') itself.

Try 'Renumberusers ?' and you will get commandline usage in C= StyleGuide
manner.

I am too lazy to write full docs for this little proggy. I think it's
better I continue work on my FullScreen Editor for TA.

If you have any ideas you think I should implement please write to me.

